# LGLC Website Templates - AI/IDE Rules

**This is the consolidated AI/IDE rules file for this project.** All AI coding assistants (Cursor, Aider, etc.) should reference this file.

This project uses a token-based design system for the Lesbian and Gay Liberation in Canada (LGLC) website templates.

**IMPORTANT:** This project follows the official **LGLC Brand Standards Manual** (`media/style_guide.pdf`).

**Digital longevity:** This project aligns with **[Project Endings](https://endings.uvic.ca/principles.html)**—[Endings Principles for Digital Longevity](https://endings.uvic.ca/principles.html) (five components: Data, Documentation, Processing, Products, Release management). When brand rules and Endings overlap (e.g. static HTML, vanilla JS, no gratuitous dependencies), treat both as requirements.

## Core Principles

1. **Follow brand standards** - Use exact colors, typography, and design elements from the official brand manual
2. **Always use design tokens** - Never hardcode CSS values. All styling must use tokens from `css/design-tokens.css`
3. **Mobile-first responsive design** - Design for mobile first, enhance for larger screens
4. **Accessibility first** - Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible and meet WCAG 2.1 standards
5. **Semantic HTML** - Use proper HTML5 elements and ARIA attributes
6. **Component isolation** - Each component in its own CSS file
7. **Endings-aligned delivery** - Prefer static, standards-based artifacts and minimal dependencies (see **Project Endings** below)

## Project Endings (digital longevity)

**Canonical reference:** [https://endings.uvic.ca/principles.html](https://endings.uvic.ca/principles.html)

Assistants should honor these project commitments when suggesting architecture, dependencies, URLs, or release practices:

### Data & documentation

- Store and exchange project data in **open, processable formats** where applicable (e.g. TEI XML, plain text, open document formats—not proprietary lock-in).
- Keep **data and documentation under version control**; treat data models (fields, meanings, controlled values) as **documented artifacts** shipped with or alongside the work.
- **Rights and licensing** should be explicit; prefer **open licenses** for data and products when possible (e.g. Creative Commons, OSI-approved licenses).

### Processing

- Prefer pipelines with **validation**: invalid inputs/outputs should fail loudly and block further steps until fixed.
- Treat **source data changes** as requiring a **full, reproducible rebuild** of site outputs when this project uses a build step; automate that where practical (**continuous integration** mindset).
- **Processing code is contingent** (not expected to last forever); still align with open standards and the same longevity goals as data and products when possible.

### Web products (templates and shipped pages)

- **Static-first:** target **static HTML + CSS + JavaScript** with **no required server-side runtime** (no database-backed pages, PHP, or Python *as part of the delivered site*). Server-side search/index tools (e.g. Solr, eXist) are an **optional enhancement** only after the static site works on its own—see concessions on the Endings page.
- **Standards, not fashion:** use **HTML5, CSS, and JavaScript** supported broadly and long-term; do not introduce **boutique stacks** or heavy client frameworks by default.
- **Minimal third-party surface:** avoid **external libraries and services** (e.g. jQuery, Bootstrap from CDN, proprietary widgets) unless the project explicitly approves an **Endings-style exception** (open source, widely used, ideally no transitive dependency chain)—see **4.9** on the Endings page.
- **Clean URLs:** avoid **query strings** for stable entity pages; each entity should have a **predictable, portable path** that works on any host.
- **Inclusion & redundancy:** favor shipping **documented source data** with the project where relevant; **self-contained pages** (header, nav, footer, key content) so a page remains usable even if other site assets are missing.
- **Graceful degradation:** core **content and navigation must remain usable** without JavaScript and remain **readable** without CSS (Endings **4.7**).

### Release management

- Prefer **planned, coherent releases** over endless “rolling” partial deploys; a release should be **complete and validated**.
- **Identify builds** with a **version and/or build date** in a consistent place (footer or colophon) when the project maintains that convention.
- Provide **clear citation guidance** for web resources when the project exposes it.
- **Stable URLs across editions** when content is versioned; use redirects for moved or retired resources.

### When Endings and brand rules conflict

**Brand standards and design tokens take precedence for visual identity** (colors, type, components). For **technology choices** (static site, dependencies, URLs, documentation), **Endings principles apply** unless the maintainers document a deliberate exception.

## Official Brand Standards

### Brand Colors (MUST USE EXACT VALUES)

**Primary Colors:**
- **Black:** `#000000` (CMYK: 0/0/0/100, RGB: 0/0/0)
- **Red:** `#ED1C24` (CMYK: 0/100/100/0, RGB: 237/28/36)
- **Navy:** `#1C3664` (CMYK: 100/87/33/23, RGB: 0/51/102)
- **Magenta:** `#EC008C` (CMYK: 0/100/0/0, RGB: 236/0/140)
- **Yellow:** `#F6BE38` (CMYK: 3/26/89/0, RGB: 246/190/56)
- **Light Grey:** `#E6E7E8` (CMYK: 0/0/0/10, RGB: 230/231/232)

**Secondary Colors (80% Tints):**
- **Black 80%:** `#58595B` (RGB: 88/89/91)
- **Red 80%:** `#F15B40` (RGB: 241/91/64)
- **Navy 80%:** `#445078` (RGB: 68/80/120)
- **Magenta 80%:** `#EF5BA1` (RGB: 239/91/161) - ~~Legacy color, no longer used for links~~
- **Yellow 80%:** `#F8C965` (RGB: 248/201/101)

**Secondary Colors (60% Tints):**
- **Black 60%:** `#808285`, **Red 60%:** `#F58466`, **Navy 60%:** `#6A6D8F`, **Magenta 60%:** `#F287B7`, **Yellow 60%:** `#FAD589`

### Official Typography Hierarchy

**Primary Typeface: Josefin Sans** (web-friendly)
- Available weights: Light, Light Italic, Regular, Bold, Bold Italic
- Use for: Body copy, secondary headings, tertiary headings, all UI elements

**Secondary Typeface: Aachen Std**
- Use for: Main headings ONLY (18pt+)
- Bold weight only

**Typography & Color Standards:**
- **Main Heading:** Aachen Std, Black (`#000000`), 18pt+ (`--font-size-lg`)
- **Secondary Heading:** Josefin Sans Bold, Navy (`#1C3664`), 14pt+ (`--font-size-sm`)
- **Tertiary Heading:** Josefin Sans Bold, Navy (`#1C3664`), 11pt+ (0.6875rem)
- **Body Copy:** Josefin Sans Regular, Navy (`#1C3664`), 10pt+ (0.625rem)
- **Links:** **Context-aware navy-based system** (see Link Color System section below)
- **Interactive Materials** (menus, maps, graphs): Red (`#ED1C24`) and Red 80% (`#F15B40`)

### Link Color System (Context-Aware)

**IMPORTANT:** Links use a context-aware color system for better brand harmony and accessibility.

**Default Links (on white/light backgrounds):**
- Link: Brightened Navy (`#2D5A8C`)
- Hover: Navy (`#1C3664`)
- Use: `var(--text-link)` and `var(--text-link-hover)`

**Links on Colored Backgrounds:**
- **Red backgrounds:** White (stays white on hover, background changes to Red 80%)
- **Navy backgrounds:** White (stays white on hover)
- **Black backgrounds:** White (stays white on hover)
- **Yellow backgrounds:** Navy → Black on hover
- **Grey backgrounds:** Navy → Brightened Navy on hover

**Implementation:**
```css
/* Default - auto-applies to <a> tags on light backgrounds */
a { color: var(--text-link); }

/* Use context classes for colored backgrounds */
<div class="bg-red"><a href="#">White link</a></div>
<div class="bg-navy"><a href="#">White link</a></div>
<section class="team-section"><a href="#">Navy link on yellow</a></section>
```

**📖 Full Documentation:** See `LINK-COLOR-SYSTEM.md` for complete specifications and usage examples.

### Logo Usage Don'ts

❌ **NEVER:**
- Stretch the logo horizontally or vertically
- Place the logo on an angle
- Reconfigure the logo elements
- Use effects like drop shadows on the logo
- Change the logo colors

## CSS Rules

### Design Token Usage

**✅ DO:**
- Always use design tokens via `var(--token-name)`
- Reference tokens from `css/design-tokens.css`
- Use semantic token names when available (`--text-primary` over `--color-primary-black`)

**❌ DON'T:**
- Never hardcode values (no `16px`, `#ED1C24`, `8px`, etc.)
- Never use raw `px` values for spacing, fonts, or sizes (except border widths which are already in tokens)
- Never define custom values in component CSS files

### CSS File Structure

1. **Import order is critical:**
   ```html
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/design-tokens.css">
   <link rel="stylesheet" href="css/your-component.css">
   ```

2. **Component files:**
   - Each component gets its own CSS file in `css/` directory
   - Import `design-tokens.css` first in HTML
   - Use design tokens exclusively

3. **Units:**
   - Use `rem` for all scalable values (spacing, fonts, sizes) via tokens
   - Use `px` ONLY for border widths (already defined in tokens)
   - Never mix units

### Example CSS:
```css
/* ✅ Correct */
.my-component {
  padding: var(--spacing-4);
  color: var(--color-primary-red);
  border-radius: var(--border-radius-md);
  font-size: var(--font-size-lg);
}

/* ❌ Incorrect */
.my-component {
  padding: 16px;
  color: #ED1C24;
  border-radius: 8px;
  font-size: 18px;
}
```

## HTML Rules

### Semantic HTML
- Use semantic HTML5 elements: `<header>`, `<main>`, `<footer>`, `<nav>`, `<article>`, `<section>`
- Include ARIA labels where needed
- Use proper heading hierarchy (h1 → h2 → h3)

### Structure
- No inline styles - keep all CSS in stylesheets
- Import CSS in correct order (design-tokens.css first)
- Include `js/header.js` before closing `</body>` tag

## JavaScript Rules

### File Organization
- Component-specific JS in `js/` directory
- Keep JavaScript vanilla (no frameworks)
- Ensure accessibility features (keyboard navigation, ARIA updates)

### Accessibility
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
- Include focus management
- Provide screen reader announcements where needed

## Component Creation Guidelines

### When creating a new component:

1. **Create CSS file:**
   - New file in `css/` directory
   - Name it descriptively (e.g., `card.css`, `button.css`)

2. **Use design tokens:**
   - Reference existing tokens via `var(--token-name)`
   - If you need a new value, add it to `css/design-tokens.css` first
   - Never define custom values in component CSS

3. **Follow existing patterns:**
   - Look at `css/header.css` and `css/footer.css` for examples
   - Maintain consistency with existing components

## Design Token Categories

### Colors (Brand Standards Compliant)
- **Primary:** 
  - `--color-primary-black` (#000000) - Main headings
  - `--color-primary-red` (#ED1C24) - Header, interactive materials
  - `--color-primary-navy` (#1C3664) - Body copy, secondary headings
  - `--color-primary-magenta` (#EC008C) - Accent elements
  - `--color-primary-yellow` (#F6BE38) - Accents, highlights
  - `--color-grey-light` (#E6E7E8) - Page backgrounds
  
- **Tints (80% and 60%):**
  - `--color-magenta-80` (#EF5BA1) - ~~Legacy, no longer used for links~~
  - `--color-red-80` (#F15B40) - Interactive materials
  - `--color-navy-80`, `--color-black-80`, `--color-yellow-80`
  - `--color-*-60` variants for 60% tints
  
- **Semantic:** 
  - `--text-primary` → Black (#000000) - Main headings (Aachen)
  - `--text-secondary` → Navy (#1C3664) - Body copy, secondary headings (Josefin)
  - `--text-tertiary` → Navy 60% (#6A6D8F) - Less important text
  - `--text-link` → Brightened Navy (#2D5A8C) - **DEFAULT LINKS** (context-aware system)
  - `--text-link-on-red`, `--text-link-on-navy`, etc. → Context-specific link colors
  - `--text-inverse` → White - Text on dark backgrounds
  
- **Backgrounds:** 
  - `--bg-page` → Light Grey (#E6E7E8)
  - `--bg-surface` → White
  - `--bg-elevated` → White

### Spacing
- Use `--spacing-1` through `--spacing-24` (0.25rem to 6rem)
- Never hardcode spacing values

### Typography (Brand Standards Compliant)
- **Font Families:**
  - `--font-family-primary`: Josefin Sans (body, secondary/tertiary headings, UI)
  - `--font-family-heading`: Aachen Std (main headings ONLY, 18pt+)
  
- **Brand Typography Hierarchy:**
  - `--font-size-main-heading`: 1.125rem (18pt+) - Aachen Std, Black
  - `--font-size-secondary-heading`: 0.875rem (14pt+) - Josefin Sans Bold, Navy
  - `--font-size-tertiary-heading`: 0.6875rem (11pt) - Josefin Sans Bold, Navy
  - `--font-size-body`: 0.625rem (10pt+) - Josefin Sans Regular, Navy
  
- **Extended Font Sizes:** `--font-size-xs` through `--font-size-5xl`
- **Font Weights:** `--font-weight-normal` (400) through `--font-weight-extrabold` (800)
- **Line Heights:** `--line-height-tight`, `--line-height-normal`, `--line-height-relaxed`, `--line-height-loose`

### Borders
- Widths: `--border-width-thin`, `--border-width-medium`, `--border-width-thick`
- Radius: `--border-radius-sm` through `--border-radius-2xl`
- Colors: `--border-color-*`

### Shadows
- `--shadow-xs` through `--shadow-2xl`

## Responsive Design

### Breakpoints
- Mobile-first approach (default styles for mobile)
- Tablet: `48rem` (768px) - use `@media (min-width: 48rem)`
- Desktop: `64rem` (1024px) - use `@media (min-width: 64rem)`
- Large Desktop: `80rem` (1280px) - use `@media (min-width: 80rem)`

**Note:** CSS variables cannot be used in `@media` queries, so use the values directly with comments:
```css
@media (min-width: 48rem) {  /* --breakpoint-md */
  /* Tablet styles */
}
```

## Accessibility Requirements

### Focus States
- Always include: Yellow outline (`--color-primary-yellow`)
- Adequate offset (`--outline-offset-sm`)
- Visible on all interactive elements

### Touch Targets
- Minimum size: `var(--touch-target-min)` (2.75rem/44px)
- Ensure buttons and links have sufficient clickable area

### Keyboard Navigation
- All interactive elements must be keyboard accessible
- Logical tab order
- Skip links for main content
- ARIA labels where needed

## Button Guidelines

### Primary Button (`.btn-primary`)
- Use for: Main call-to-action, primary user actions
- Black background (`--color-primary-black`), white text
- Focus: Yellow outline

### Secondary Button (`.btn-secondary`)
- Use for: Secondary actions, alternative options
- Transparent background, black text, gray border
- Focus: Yellow outline

## Card Guidelines

### Content Cards (`.card`)
- White background
- Use for: Content previews, feature highlights, grid layouts
- Hover: Slight lift, enhanced shadow
- Focus: Yellow outline

### Related Results Cards (`.related-card`)
- Use for: Related content on detail pages
- Icon/image at top, heading, list of items
- 3-column grid on desktop

## Typography Guidelines

### Font Sizes
- **5xl (3rem)**: Hero titles, landing page main headings
- **4xl (2.25rem)**: Section titles, major page headings
- **3xl (1.875rem)**: Subsection headings, large content titles
- **2xl (1.5rem)**: Medium headings, section subheadings
- **xl (1.25rem)**: Small headings, card titles
- **lg (1.125rem)**: Large body text, emphasized content
- **base (1rem)**: Default body text, buttons, form inputs
- **sm (0.875rem)**: Small text, captions, metadata
- **xs (0.75rem)**: Tiny text, fine print

### Font Weights
- **Extrabold (800)**: Hero titles, major emphasis
- **Bold (700)**: Section headings, important content
- **Semibold (600)**: Buttons, card titles, emphasized text
- **Medium (500)**: Navigation links, subheadings
- **Normal (400)**: Body text, default weight

## Layout Patterns

### Containers
- `.landing-container`: Landing page sections (max-width: 75rem)
- `.record-container`: Individual record pages (max-width: 80rem)
- `.search-section`: Search page content (max-width: 72.5rem)

### Grids
- `.cards-grid`: 3-column grid, stacks to 1 column on mobile
- Gap: `--spacing-8`

## File Structure

```
├── css/
│   ├── design-tokens.css    # Design system (MUST be imported first)
│   ├── header.css
│   ├── footer.css
│   ├── landing.css
│   ├── records.css
│   └── search.css
├── js/
│   └── header.js
├── media/                   # Images and assets
├── index.html               # Main template
└── search.html              # Search page template
```

## Quick Reference

### Common Mistakes to Avoid
1. ❌ Hardcoding CSS values instead of using tokens
2. ❌ Using `px` for spacing/fonts instead of `rem` via tokens
3. ❌ Defining custom values in component CSS files
4. ❌ Importing CSS files in wrong order
5. ❌ Using inline styles
6. ❌ Creating components without checking existing patterns
7. ❌ Not including accessibility features (focus states, ARIA)
8. ❌ Making touch targets too small (< 44px)
9. ❌ Introducing server-side page generation, databases, or heavy third-party client stacks as required dependencies (conflicts with [Project Endings](https://endings.uvic.ca/principles.html) unless maintainers document an exception)

### When in Doubt
- **Check brand standards:** `media/style_guide.pdf` for official colors, typography, and logo usage
- **Check Endings principles:** [endings.uvic.ca/principles.html](https://endings.uvic.ca/principles.html) for digital longevity (static-first, minimal dependencies, clean URLs, documented data, release discipline)
- **Check design language:** `DESIGN-LANGUAGE.md` for detailed component guidelines and brand implementation
- Check `css/design-tokens.css` for available tokens
- Look at existing components (`css/header.css`, `css/footer.css`) for patterns
- Refer to `README.md` for project structure and usage

## Brand Standards Summary

**Critical Brand Rules:**
1. ✅ Use **exact** hex values from brand palette (no approximations)
2. ✅ Use **Aachen Std** for main headings ONLY (18pt+, Black)
3. ✅ Use **Josefin Sans** for all other text (Regular/Bold, Navy for body/headings)
4. ✅ Use **context-aware link color system** (navy-based, see `LINK-COLOR-SYSTEM.md`)
5. ✅ Use **Navy** (#1C3664) for body copy and secondary headings
6. ✅ Use **Red** (#ED1C24) and **Red 80%** (#F15B40) for interactive materials
7. ✅ Use **Light Grey** (#E6E7E8) for page backgrounds
8. ❌ NEVER stretch, rotate, or apply effects to logos
9. ❌ NEVER use colors outside the approved brand palette
10. ❌ NEVER use Josefin Sans for main headings (use Aachen Std)
11. ❌ NEVER hardcode link colors - use `var(--text-link)` and context tokens

**For complete brand guidelines, see:**
- Official Brand Standards Manual: `media/style_guide.pdf`
- Design Language Documentation: `DESIGN-LANGUAGE.md`
- Link Color System: `LINK-COLOR-SYSTEM.md` ← **NEW: Context-aware link colors**
- Brand-compliant Design Tokens: `css/design-tokens.css`

## Quick Checklist

Before suggesting code, ensure:
- [ ] Uses design tokens (no hardcoded values)
- [ ] CSS import order is correct (design-tokens.css first)
- [ ] Semantic HTML is used
- [ ] Accessibility features included (focus, ARIA, keyboard nav)
- [ ] Responsive design (mobile-first)
- [ ] Follows existing component patterns
- [ ] No inline styles
- [ ] Touch targets are adequate (44px minimum)
- [ ] Endings-aligned: static HTML/CSS/JS bias; no new heavy frameworks or CDN dependencies without explicit project approval
- [ ] Core content works without JavaScript; readable without CSS where applicable
- [ ] Entity URLs avoid query strings when the project uses stable record pages

